    <h1 class="text-4xl tracking-tight uppercase font-bold text-white mb-6" style="letter-spacing: 0.1em;">Punjab Data Project</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-4">A computational sociological analysis of British Punjab through the imperial print register, 1867–1942. With Prof. Emmett Davis.</p>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 mb-12">Under Act XXV of 1867, every book, pamphlet and handbill printed in British India had to be registered. The result is a quarterly printed catalogue kept for seventy-five years — the most complete surviving record of what was printed in colonial South Asia, existing today only as scanned images of a ruled bureaucratic table. Not searchable, not countable, not usable as data. This project converts it.</p>

